  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA/AFRICOM Workshop 01-22: &quot;Countering Violent Extremism: The Evolution of Radicalization and Responses&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In examining radicalization in the region two issues come to the forefront: the continuing and evolving use of social media as a preferred tool used by extremist groups for propaganda and recruiting and the increasing challenges dealing with returning foreign fighters. Countering terrorism and countering violent extremist is a complex, multi-dimensional challenge. As such it requires a comprehensive &quot;whole of government&quot; and &quot;whole of society&quot; approach. It also addresses the new and persistent challenges effectively dealing with returning foreign fighters, their spouses and their children, as well as preventing radicalization.</narrative>
  </description>
